What is the entity for the "Plus-Minus" symbol (±)?
A)&pm;
B)&plusmn;//answer
C)&plus-minus;
D)&pmn;

✅ Correct Answer: B. &plusmn;

Explanation (Simple)

The HTML entity for the Plus-Minus (±) symbol is:

&plusmn;

It displays as:

±

Example:
<p>Temperature: 25&plusmn;2&deg;C</p>

Output:

Temperature: 25±2°C
Why not the others?
❌ A. &pm; → Not a valid HTML entity.
✅ B. &plusmn; → Correct! Displays ±.
❌ C. &plus-minus; → Not a valid HTML entity.
❌ D. &pmn; → Not a valid HTML entity.

✅ Correct Answer: B. &plusmn;


